Z||000000||shiloh187||03-28-2001||12:34 AM||||okay here is where i am at...  the guy who is working on my POS i just bought was about to change the oil and it looks like the pan was dented.. he got it off but the threading was all rusted so the bolt would not go back in.. we got a new piece for like $8.. no big deal..<P>to put it back togehter, he says the whole damn engine has to come out basically so my question is, while it is all apart, what should i replace so that i dont need to later in time, and approx cost of these things?<P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||03-28-2001||02:58 AM||||Figures, huh? Been there, done that, owned a Mazda (At least until some twit left a fridge door lying on the highway... But that's a different story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>I'd consider the timing chain/timing gears (v6, L4), and check the bottom-end bearings.<P>This is all assuming that most of the regular maintenance stuff has been done. Also, if it's a STD, consider a new clutch, since it's already out, and simple to replace at that point.||||reg||8
Z||000002||shiloh187||03-28-2001||04:28 AM||||well with all the problems i have been having, i am going to assume this car has 70k miles and a poor maintenenace record... so far everything has gone wrong that can.. i paid $1000 for it because i need a car to get me to and from work, and have not een able to drive it yet...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>so with that in mind, what should i do while he has it out to do whatever he has to do to the oil pan...<P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||03-28-2001||05:57 AM||||The pan can be replaced without pulling the engine. the engine can be supported, exhaust system loosened, front motor mount and starter removed and it will come out. <BR>With some minor differences this applys to both 2.5 and 2.8.||||reg||1
Z||000004||shiloh187||03-28-2001||04:11 PM||||thank you... anything else i should replace now besides them things?<P>shiloh<BR>||||reg||1
